{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The wicked</b> — the opposite of the righteous. When he sees the wealth of the righteous, he is angered out of great envy." "<b>His teeth</b> — according to his thought, that he will yet grind his teeth to take vengeance. And this will be, for all this shall melt away — that which he thinks. And thus is the desire of the wicked: they desire evil for the good."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 112, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:30.986417969Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}